// SUPERSEDED 2026-08-29 (the bottom-ride deletion): the ride this
// fixture pinned is gone. A bottom scrutinee now BOTTOMS the select on
// both engines (no held-arm ride), so this program agrees by bottoming
// out. The historical description below documents the deleted behavior.
//
// Quiet-scrutinee body-driven fire (aug06ghz0 reactive, Eric's
// ruling 2026-08-07): selection is OBSERVABLE MEMORY — a STANDING
// selection whose scrutinee delivers nothing this cycle (the fold
// div0-bottoms, so v2 is tainted in the kernel) still fires when the
// taken arm's body fires on its own deps. Epoch 1 injects in0=0 and
// epoch 2 injects in0=7: the select must emit the FRESH values (0
// then 7 — body production, not a ride). Pre-fix the phantom-arm
// gate (0a0014eb) routed every tainted-scrutinee take to miss —
// conflating never-selected with selected-but-quiet — and the jit
// swallowed both fires. Under THE UNIFIED RIDE (Eric's ruling
// 2026-08-28, superseding the 2026-08-07 scrutinee VALUE cache) a
// bottom scrutinee HOLDS the last selection by INDEX (no cache, no
// pattern re-match) and jumps to the held arm; its bind (v2) comes out
// bottom but the body reads in0, which fires on its own deps, so the
// arm emits the fresh value. A never-selected hold has no index and
// still routes to miss (the aug04b phantom rule preserved).
// schedule-v1: cap=96 events=768; in0=i64:0; in0=i64:7
{
	let v0: Array<i64> = [];
	v0 <- in0 ~ array::push(v0, i64:0);
	let v3: i64 = {
		let v2: u8 = array::fold(v0, u8:0, |a, x| (a / a));
		select v2 { _ => in0 }
	};
	v3
}